                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Whisper of a Rose, developed by RosePortal Games and published by KOMODO, is an independent fantasy RPG that demonstrates how a compelling story can leave a lasting impression even without cutting-edge visuals or blockbuster production values. Built with a clear appreciation for classic Japanese role-playing games, it tells the tale of Melrose, a young girl whose difficult home life drives her to seek comfort in dreams. What begins as an escape from bullying and neglect gradually unfolds into a much larger adventure when she discovers that the world she has imagined is real and in desperate need of her help. The result is a game that blends traditional fantasy elements with surprisingly mature themes centered on loneliness, acceptance, and finding one's place in the world.\n\nUnlike many RPGs that immediately focus on saving kingdoms or defeating ancient evils, Whisper of a Rose spends considerable time establishing its protagonist and her emotional struggles. Melrose is easy to sympathize with because her problems feel grounded despite the fantastical setting surrounding her. As the narrative progresses, players encounter a colorful cast of allies and adversaries, each contributing to a world that feels alive and interconnected. The game explores the relationship between dreams and reality in ways that elevate its story beyond a standard coming-of-age adventure. While some dialogue occasionally leans toward melodrama, the sincerity of its writing helps many of its emotional moments land effectively.\n\nFrom a gameplay perspective, Whisper of a Rose remains firmly rooted in old-school RPG traditions. Turn-based battles, character progression, equipment management, and exploration form the core experience. The game expands upon these familiar mechanics with a sizeable skill tree system, crafting options, hidden collectibles, side quests, and environmental puzzles. There is an impressive amount of content available, giving players dozens of hours to immerse themselves in Melrose's journey. Character customization allows for different approaches to combat, making progression feel rewarding despite the relatively straightforward battle system.\n\nExploration is another highlight. The dream world is composed of numerous locations that each possess their own personality, ranging from peaceful settlements and enchanted forests to ominous ruins and mysterious underwater realms. Although the title was created with modest tools, the developers make effective use of their resources to ensure each environment feels distinct. The soundtrack further enhances these areas, shifting comfortably between whimsical melodies and more somber compositions depending on the situation. Together, the music and setting create an atmosphere that captures the spirit of classic role-playing adventures from earlier gaming generations.\n\nHowever, the game's ambitions occasionally exceed its technical limitations. Combat encounters can become repetitive during extended sessions, and some dungeons overstay their welcome due to their size and pacing. The user interface and visual presentation are also products of their time, and players accustomed to modern conveniences may find certain aspects dated. There are moments when the narrative slows considerably, particularly when juggling optional content alongside the main quest. Nevertheless, these shortcomings are easier to forgive when viewed in the context of the game's independent development and evident passion.\n\nWhat ultimately makes Whisper of a Rose memorable is its willingness to tell an intimate story through the framework of a traditional RPG. It is less concerned with reinventing genre conventions and more interested in delivering a heartfelt experience that resonates emotionally. RosePortal Games clearly poured considerable effort into creating a world filled with secrets, memorable encounters, and themes that extend beyond the fantasy setting itself. Players who enjoy narrative-driven adventures and appreciate the charm of classic RPG Maker titles will likely find much to admire here.\n\nWhisper of a Rose may not appeal to everyone, especially those seeking fast-paced gameplay or contemporary production standards, but it succeeds in offering an adventure with genuine heart. Its blend of extensive content, endearing characters, and emotional storytelling ensures that Melrose's journey remains memorable long after it concludes. For fans of traditional role-playing games, it stands as an underrated title worthy of recognition.\n\nRating: 6/10",
